---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'About & Verification Standards | Field Season HQ';
const description = 'How Field Season HQ compiles, verifies, and cites official 2026–2027 state hunting season dates, licensing rules, and draw deadlines.';
const canonical = 'https://fieldseasonhq.com/about/';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <section class="about-section"><div class="container prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">Methodology</span>
    <h1>About Field Season HQ</h1>
    <p class="last-verified">Last updated: November 22, 2026</p>

    <p>Field Season HQ (fieldseasonhq.com) is an independent hunting season reference built to give hunters fast, clean access to statewide season dates, legal hunting methods, licensing basics, and draw deadlines without popups or clutter.</p>

    <h2>How We Verify Hunting Regulations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Primary Government Sources Only:</strong> Every season window, license requirement, and application deadline is compiled directly from official state wildlife agency regulation booklets, administrative codes, and licensing portals.</li>
      <li><strong>Row-Level Citations:</strong> Each fact in our tables includes a direct link to the governing agency source and its verification date so you can confirm unit-specific rules in one click.</li>
      <li><strong>Always Confirm Before You Hunt:</strong> Wildlife commissions periodically issue emergency closures, chronic wasting disease (CWD) transport updates, or quota adjustments. Always verify your exact hunt unit with the state agency before going afield.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
    <p><strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong></p>
    <p>Field Season HQ includes curated field gear checklists matched to state species and visibility rules. Clicking an Amazon product link does not add any extra cost to your purchase. For full details, see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy &amp; Affiliate Disclosure</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
